measurements.what:
Core, engineering only, before the freeze. Measures:
- hooked decode at batch 32 and 0.5-1.1k context with the full capture set;
- R1 / R3 read rates;
- B = 1 16k / 32k prefill with hooks;
- duet re-prefill cost and carried-cache parity;
- RefKL hooks time;
- Drive throughput.
Uses stand-in random sets; the texts are excluded from all analyses. Defines G-pilot and freezes the cost table.

Core. Known-answer calibration on synthetic data at the planned sizes, items (a)-(n):
- PIP tree;
- item-stratified stickiness and HD rank test;
- within-item bistability;
- static and kinetic Ising;
- EQMI growth classifier;
- length-against-information slopes;
- irreversibility d-hat against a detailed-balance band;
- RQA difference-in-differences;
- cross-map;
- agent J_ex with item fields;
- pair-macro Delta Psi;
- ownership classifier with chance matches;
- step-error conditional hazard.
A failed item makes the dependent verdicts 'not testable (pipeline calibration failed)'.

Core; code and associative-memory senses. Is the hallucination signal in the H-neurons a local store, one of several representations, distributed, dense, or holographic-like? Tools:
- PIP over uniform, matched (99), rotated-basis and excluding-H fragments, with a permutation floor at every size;
- knock-out reselection;
- onset synergy against a dense reference and bias-corrected I3 monogamy;
- latent scalars;
- pre-answer PIP;
- planted-code calibration on the real CETT matrix.
Also causal erasure with the model as decoder (nested random mean-ablations 2^-12..2^-4, P, and 8 damage-matched sets with set-level resampling): threshold against graceful degradation, and causal privilege. Flags: 'not a strict threshold code (falsified)', selection robustness over K's 20 bootstrap H-sets.

