J1 fatal flaw, lean L4 (item confound and push-active probes). Fixed by:
- item fixed effects plus the coupling statistic J_ex = excess over within-(item, configuration) re-pairing, with item-cluster bootstrap;
- 4 seeds per item-configuration to allow re-pairing;
- context-free stance readout by the unmodified model, so the push never touches the readout.
Merge simulations: item FE alone gave a 0.44 false-positive rate at item-field SD 1.0 (sim_duet.py); J_ex is unbiased (sim_duet2.py).

J1 fatal flaw, lean R-L2c (interface matching no K design). Fixed by:
- L5 built on K's exact-label arithmetic records;
- an explicit K.LENS-OUT / K.ITEMS-ARITH contract with K-lean and K-mechanism names, and gate G-CL.

Holographic fatal flaws avoided in grafted parts:
- pooled-surrogate frailty: lean's item-specific surrogates used;
- mechanical in-window K denominator: R1 turn reads, and X1 retention uses a post-release early window;
- P_H hull against an unhulled P_SEL: SEL+ and UNC+ hull-matched;
- EOS masking: chains allow EOS; only raw book continuation masks it, stated;
- entity OR rule: a single primary entity criterion;
- across-setting cross-pairing: within-item re-pairing;
- L1a chance matches: foreign-M_j null, M_i from greedy and T 0.7 only.

Energy_ising fatal flaws avoided:
- 'self-sustaining' without K > 1: R6 on a pooled 5-turn carry;
- pooled HD: Mantel-Haenszel over item x bin;
- contradictory entity reading: merge = supports the chain link, two entities = against;
- L11 TriviaQA overlap requirement: L5 on K's arithmetic items;
- uncalibrated L9(c): L1 planted calibration.

J2 lean defects fixed:
- R-L2a replaced;
- R-L2b given within-chain demeaning;
- BI added;
- entropy used as covariate and as the E-channel;
- Delta K margin set to 0.40 >= MDE 0.34;
- 'Who' label gated by G-sel;
- D.LONGCORPUS fallback;
- L4 re-costed with re-prefill (34.4 min);
- L1-C re-costed (15 min with 3 seeds and fewer K.SELECT calls);
- K.CETTMAT copy-in replaced by an in-session recompute (2 min).

Missing everywhere, uncertainty as common driver (J1, J2). Added:
- UNC+, selected by K's pipeline for a within-class entropy label;
- the E-channel;
- an entropy covariate in the hazard, length and step-error models;
- the qualifier 'not beyond uncertainty'.

Missing everywhere, dose ladder and hysteresis (J1, J2):
- X1 with matched H-low / H-high starts and alpha ladders, post-release retention, capture and hysteresis verdicts;
- a frozen reading that reconciles the designs: restoring is local stability and counts for nothing; capture beyond a threshold is attractor evidence.

Missing everywhere, power of the conjunctive combined verdicts (J2):
- simulated in sim_combined*.py and sim_own2.py (table in L.5);
- the first rule structure gave the correct label only about half the time, so L3 was split into an attractor line and a specificity line, and equivalence margins were set near 2.9 SE;
- correct labels now come out in 0.64-0.86 of runs in clear scenarios, and 0.32 for a weak K_H = 1.15.
